WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.379 --> 00:00:01.531
- [Kelly] You can sit wherever you'd like.

00:00:01.531 --> 00:00:02.364
I like your pants.

00:00:02.364 --> 00:00:03.197
- I was told to sit in the middle.

00:00:03.197 --> 00:00:04.171
Thanks, they don't belong to me.

00:00:04.171 --> 00:00:05.180
- Oh, you know, yeah.

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:07.040
I'll give this back too, I get you.

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:07.873
We can only wear it once.

00:00:07.873 --> 00:00:08.706
- [Colin] Do you get to
keep some stuff though?

00:00:08.706 --> 00:00:09.539
- Sometimes I keep it,

00:00:09.539 --> 00:00:11.061
because I'll probably
keep the shirt, yeah.

00:00:11.061 --> 00:00:11.894
- Yeah, it's really cool.

00:00:11.894 --> 00:00:12.727
I was thinking that when you were singing.

00:00:12.727 --> 00:00:16.558
- Yeah, I keep the like,
really casual stuff, Colin.

00:00:16.558 --> 00:00:17.941
I don't keep the dresses.

00:00:17.941 --> 00:00:19.101
Wait, so I love music so much,

00:00:19.101 --> 00:00:20.832
but I love asking people
that come on the show,

00:00:20.832 --> 00:00:21.832
like, what you're listening to?

00:00:21.832 --> 00:00:22.729
Like what are you into?

00:00:22.729 --> 00:00:25.260
- Oh God, I listen to everything.

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:27.641
I listen to anything from Elvis to...

00:00:27.641 --> 00:00:28.582
- Oh.
- U2.

00:00:28.582 --> 00:00:30.904
- I almost gave you Elvis vinyl.

00:00:30.904 --> 00:00:31.737
Dang it.

00:00:31.737 --> 00:00:33.178
I almost gave you Elvis vinyl.

00:00:33.178 --> 00:00:34.613
- [Colin] I saw there
was a record in the bag.

00:00:34.613 --> 00:00:35.792
- Did I give you Chris Stapleton?

00:00:35.792 --> 00:00:36.625
- No.

00:00:36.625 --> 00:00:37.733
- Did I? What did I end up with?

00:00:37.733 --> 00:00:39.733
I had so many options for
you and I was like going,

00:00:39.733 --> 00:00:40.752
it's always hard to get...

00:00:40.752 --> 00:00:42.352
- I'm grateful for it anyway,
because I have vinyls at home.

00:00:42.352 --> 00:00:43.185
Thank you.

00:00:43.185 --> 00:00:44.018
- [Kelly] Yeah, yeah.

00:00:44.018 --> 00:00:44.851
- But I love everything.

00:00:44.851 --> 00:00:45.752
- I didn't give you Johnny,
I almost gave you Elvis,

00:00:45.752 --> 00:00:46.918
but I didn't give you Johnny.

00:00:46.918 --> 00:00:48.020
- John Lee Hooker, you know?

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:49.531
- [Kelly] Yeah, well next time.

00:00:49.531 --> 00:00:50.600
- Some EDM.

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:51.588
- Oh, I like EDM.

00:00:51.588 --> 00:00:53.640
Oh, I gave you Cage The Elephant.

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:54.909
- Oh, that's exactly what you gave me.

00:00:54.909 --> 00:00:55.742
- [Kelly] I gave you Cage The Elephant.

00:00:55.742 --> 00:00:56.575
That's who I gave you, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:56.575 --> 00:00:57.408
- What is that? Who is that?

00:00:57.408 --> 00:00:58.241
- [Kelly] Oh, you didn't
know Cage The Elephant?

00:00:58.241 --> 00:00:59.180
- No, I don't, it's a
good journey of discovery.

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:00.013
- Well, you're welcome.

00:01:00.013 --> 00:01:00.846
- Yeah, it's a journey of discovery.

00:01:00.846 --> 00:01:01.679
- Journey of discovery.
- Thank you.

00:01:01.679 --> 00:01:02.512
- No, I like to like,

00:01:02.512 --> 00:01:03.605
either give people things they might like,

00:01:03.605 --> 00:01:05.464
or maybe something I
think they might like.

00:01:05.464 --> 00:01:07.744
- And is that in the bent
of EDM? Is it electronic?

00:01:07.744 --> 00:01:09.304
- [Kelly] I mean its like, its just a,

00:01:09.304 --> 00:01:10.264
I don't know, it's like cool music.

00:01:10.264 --> 00:01:11.097
- [Colin] Is it like safari?

00:01:11.097 --> 00:01:11.930
- [Kelly] It's a cool, alternative music.

00:01:11.930 --> 00:01:13.596
It's like you're on a
safari. (Kelly laughs)

00:01:13.596 --> 00:01:14.645
- [Colin] Like Massive Attack or?

00:01:14.645 --> 00:01:15.478
Like Massive Attack or no?

00:01:15.478 --> 00:01:16.645
- [Kelly] No, no, it's a little different.

00:01:16.645 --> 00:01:18.293
- Not that I'm saying that
Massive Attack are EDM.

00:01:18.293 --> 00:01:19.126
- [Kelly] I mean, you might like it,

00:01:19.126 --> 00:01:20.154
you might, you might not, I don't know.

00:01:20.154 --> 00:01:21.085
- But "Hamilton", come on,

00:01:21.085 --> 00:01:22.104
we're going straight to "Hamilton".

00:01:22.104 --> 00:01:22.937
Let's not beat around the bush.

00:01:22.937 --> 00:01:23.770
- [Kelly] Oh "Hamilton",
I love "Hamilton".

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:25.143
- I know you love "Hamilton", I was told.

00:01:25.143 --> 00:01:25.976
- [Kelly] Yes, I was on the soundtrack.

00:01:25.976 --> 00:01:27.904
- I know you were on the
soundtrack, I was told.

00:01:27.904 --> 00:01:28.952
No, I wasn't told, I was told,

00:01:28.952 --> 00:01:30.234
but by the time I was told, I knew,

00:01:30.234 --> 00:01:31.542
because I'd heard it so many times.

00:01:31.542 --> 00:01:33.914
Because your version of "Quiet Uptown",

00:01:33.914 --> 00:01:36.922
is so, I mean, the original version,

00:01:36.922 --> 00:01:38.474
all of the cast's versions are fantastic.

00:01:38.474 --> 00:01:41.693
But your version on the
mix tape is extraordinary.

00:01:41.693 --> 00:01:42.526
- Thank you.
(audience applauds)

00:01:42.526 --> 00:01:43.973
- [Colin] I sound like I'm
trying to say the right thing.

00:01:43.973 --> 00:01:45.562
Have you heard it?
(audience applauds)

00:01:45.562 --> 00:01:46.681
I try to say the right thing,

00:01:46.681 --> 00:01:47.901
I ingratiate myself to you,

00:01:47.901 --> 00:01:49.333
but I promise, I'm not trying to do that.

00:01:49.333 --> 00:01:50.432
I have heard it so many times.

00:01:50.432 --> 00:01:53.272
I've asked and a few people,
I was going to say so many,

00:01:53.272 --> 00:01:54.493
but that's not true, but a few,

00:01:54.493 --> 00:01:56.614
a few is a lot in this kind
of thing. (Kelly laughs)

00:01:56.614 --> 00:01:58.506
To have a listen of it, to it.
- Yeah.

00:01:58.506 --> 00:01:59.693
- It's so moving, I mean, you're just...

00:01:59.693 --> 00:02:00.526
- [Kelly] Oh, thank you.

00:02:00.526 --> 00:02:04.264
- Such an ability to, you
must be very empathetic.

00:02:04.264 --> 00:02:05.384
- I am very empathetic, it's annoying.

00:02:05.384 --> 00:02:08.362
- [Colin] You must be
because it's very hard, yeah.

00:02:08.362 --> 00:02:09.629
But it's very hard not to
feel you, when you're singing.

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:11.400
It's extraordinary and that song...

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:12.569
- Well, that song...
- Is painful.

00:02:12.569 --> 00:02:13.402
- It is painful.

00:02:13.402 --> 00:02:15.550
Especially, when I had not seen "Hamilton"

00:02:15.550 --> 00:02:16.851
and I had no idea what it was about

00:02:16.851 --> 00:02:18.401
and they sent it to me and they're like,

00:02:18.401 --> 00:02:20.021
"Oh, they were thinking
maybe you could do this".

00:02:20.021 --> 00:02:21.169
- [Colin] They sent you the play shots?

00:02:21.169 --> 00:02:22.781
- [Kelly] No, no, no, they
just sent me the song, right?

00:02:22.781 --> 00:02:23.614
- Yeah.

00:02:23.614 --> 00:02:25.281
- I'm pregnant with my son.

00:02:25.281 --> 00:02:27.531
I'm literally pregnant, like with my son

00:02:27.531 --> 00:02:29.211
and to hear that song for the first time,

00:02:29.211 --> 00:02:30.851
I called my label...
- What trimester?

00:02:30.851 --> 00:02:32.310
What trimester? That could be dangerous.

00:02:32.310 --> 00:02:33.841
- About to pop, about to pop.

00:02:33.841 --> 00:02:35.959
I'm so afraid of a
miscarriage, I'm terrified.

00:02:35.959 --> 00:02:38.142
No, literally, I'm stressed.

00:02:38.142 --> 00:02:39.731
And I heard this and I
called him like, just crying.

00:02:39.731 --> 00:02:41.297
I was like, who...
(beeping)

00:02:41.297 --> 00:02:43.330
Sends this to someone?
(audience laughs)

00:02:43.330 --> 00:02:45.910
Like who does to someone,
like when they're pregnant...

00:02:45.910 --> 00:02:46.743
- It's brutal.

00:02:46.743 --> 00:02:47.612
- And it's so brutal, but I will say,

00:02:47.612 --> 00:02:49.310
I ended up with Jason
over there, our producer

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:50.772
and we did it like, while I was pregnant.

00:02:50.772 --> 00:02:54.630
And I think because of that,
it came across so real,

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:56.281
I think because I was terrified.

00:02:56.281 --> 00:02:57.340
- I think it would've...
(beeping)

00:02:57.340 --> 00:03:00.165
If you weren't knocked up.
(Kelly and audience laugh)

00:03:00.165 --> 00:03:01.537
That's what we're saying,
I just want to be clear.

00:03:01.537 --> 00:03:03.869
- Look Colin, I'm very method.

00:03:03.869 --> 00:03:04.832
- I just want to be clear
on what we're saying.

00:03:04.832 --> 00:03:06.692
- I'm very method and so I got knocked up,

00:03:06.692 --> 00:03:07.623
purposely for this song.

00:03:07.623 --> 00:03:10.393
- Of course, that would've
added to the rawness

00:03:10.393 --> 00:03:12.564
and the fear, the sorrow of that piece.

00:03:12.564 --> 00:03:14.290
- I cried almost every
time, it's such a...

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:15.123
- [Colin] It's a really...

00:03:15.123 --> 00:03:16.522
I mean, I've seen the
show a number of times,

00:03:16.522 --> 00:03:17.393
number of times, yeah.

00:03:17.393 --> 00:03:19.222
- It's so good, I saw
it twice, it's so good.

00:03:19.222 --> 00:03:20.433
- Oh, my God, yeah.

00:03:20.433 --> 00:03:23.282
- And just that one person
created all of that.

00:03:23.282 --> 00:03:24.844
- That's the bit that spins me out.

00:03:24.844 --> 00:03:27.969
- Yeah, it all came from
your brain, it's rude.

00:03:27.969 --> 00:03:28.802
- Picked up a book.

00:03:28.802 --> 00:03:30.887
It is rude and it's ready
and he picked up a book,

00:03:30.887 --> 00:03:32.996
in the airport about Alexander Hamilton

00:03:32.996 --> 00:03:34.105
and then he thought, "Well this would make

00:03:34.105 --> 00:03:37.545
a good hip-hop, rhymey
musical for three hours.

00:03:37.545 --> 00:03:38.996
I'll take over the world with this".

00:03:38.996 --> 00:03:40.007
Yeah.
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:40.007 --> 00:03:40.935
I mean, it's astonishing.

00:03:40.935 --> 00:03:42.585
I was really, the first time I saw it,

00:03:42.585 --> 00:03:45.583
in New York city, I
was baffled by the fact

00:03:45.583 --> 00:03:49.785
that one man gave life
and breath and, and yeah.

00:03:49.785 --> 00:03:51.236
Rhyme and rhythm to this whole...

00:03:51.236 --> 00:03:52.876
And music, that he
wrote the music as well.

00:03:52.876 --> 00:03:53.825
- It's so beautiful.

00:03:53.825 --> 00:03:55.013
- God, he's so talented.

00:03:55.013 --> 00:03:56.887
But anyway, you singing that song quite...

00:03:56.887 --> 00:03:58.047
- [Kelly] It was a
treat to get to sing it.

00:03:58.047 --> 00:03:59.255
I just wish I hadn't have been...

00:03:59.255 --> 00:04:01.126
- Because you're battered
by that stage of the show.

00:04:01.126 --> 00:04:02.759
You were terrified singing it?

00:04:02.759 --> 00:04:03.592
- No, I was terrified singing it,

00:04:03.592 --> 00:04:05.450
just because I couldn't get
through it. I kept crying.

00:04:05.450 --> 00:04:06.283
- Oh, did you?

00:04:06.283 --> 00:04:07.417
- Jason was like, "You're
going to have a breakdown".

00:04:07.417 --> 00:04:08.250
(Kelly laughs)

00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:09.083
- I saw you...

00:04:09.083 --> 00:04:10.196
- Because it's so sad
about losing your son.

00:04:10.196 --> 00:04:11.697
- You get emotional when you
sing sometimes, don't you?

00:04:11.697 --> 00:04:13.664
- I, I, it's a thing that I do.

00:04:13.664 --> 00:04:14.497
- Yeah.

00:04:14.497 --> 00:04:15.721
It's gorgeous.
- It's annoying.

00:04:15.721 --> 00:04:16.554
- I bet it is annoying,

00:04:16.554 --> 00:04:17.525
I bet you feel like people think

00:04:17.525 --> 00:04:19.317
that you're putting it on and all that,

00:04:19.317 --> 00:04:20.256
because it's a cynical world.

00:04:20.256 --> 00:04:21.595
- Well, I was also pregnant another time,

00:04:21.595 --> 00:04:22.905
with another child on TV

00:04:22.905 --> 00:04:25.227
and they had me sing at
the end of this big thing.

00:04:25.227 --> 00:04:26.856
Like, it was a huge thing for my career

00:04:26.856 --> 00:04:27.925
and I cried at that too.

00:04:27.925 --> 00:04:29.276
I cry a lot, I'm very empathetic.

00:04:29.276 --> 00:04:30.227
It's annoying, anyway.

00:04:30.227 --> 00:04:31.060
- [Colin] No, it's lovely.

00:04:31.060 --> 00:04:32.043
Yeah, "Hamilton" floors me every time

00:04:32.043 --> 00:04:33.787
and "Jesus Christ Superstar" I've seen

00:04:33.787 --> 00:04:35.852
and that has moved me at times.

00:04:35.852 --> 00:04:38.727
And "Rent" used to mess me up.

00:04:38.727 --> 00:04:39.718
- [Kelly] Now, but see...

00:04:39.718 --> 00:04:40.551
- So, you're talking about,

00:04:40.551 --> 00:04:42.427
you're talking about
singing a song on "Hamilton"

00:04:42.427 --> 00:04:46.448
that is about a father
and a mother reconciling,

00:04:46.448 --> 00:04:48.768
through the grief that they've shared.

00:04:48.768 --> 00:04:49.601
- Yeah.

00:04:49.601 --> 00:04:51.856
- As a result of the death of their son.

00:04:51.856 --> 00:04:54.358
And you found that of
course, incredibly emotional,

00:04:54.358 --> 00:04:55.191
when you were pregnant.

00:04:55.191 --> 00:04:56.316
It's emotional anyway, you
don't need to be pregnant.

00:04:56.316 --> 00:04:57.149
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:57.149 --> 00:04:58.056
- I wasn't pregnant when
I found it emotional,

00:04:58.056 --> 00:04:59.776
(Kelly and audience laugh)
but I get why you did.

00:04:59.776 --> 00:05:03.038
Well, like when you, when
you have a brother, who's gay

00:05:03.038 --> 00:05:04.739
and you go and see something like "Rent"

00:05:04.739 --> 00:05:07.256
and obviously aids and
the epidemic, in New York

00:05:07.256 --> 00:05:09.176
is such a center piece of that musical.

00:05:09.176 --> 00:05:10.009
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:10.009 --> 00:05:12.667
- And like, it was like
"Philadelphia" floored me.

00:05:12.667 --> 00:05:14.187
- Oh my gosh, I couldn't keep it together.

00:05:14.187 --> 00:05:15.478
- And I think it would've anyway,

00:05:15.478 --> 00:05:17.125
but because things are so, when
things become personalized,

00:05:17.125 --> 00:05:18.907
of course, they go in deeper, you know?

00:05:18.907 --> 00:05:20.376
- And even speaking to
something that's happening,

00:05:20.376 --> 00:05:21.209
in society.

00:05:21.209 --> 00:05:22.494
- [Colin] Yeah, absolutely, absolutely.

00:05:22.494 --> 00:05:23.643
It opens it up even wider.

00:05:23.643 --> 00:05:25.427
- But just so you know,
his name is Colt Smith

00:05:25.427 --> 00:05:27.206
and he ruined "Rent" for me.
(Kelly laughs)

00:05:27.206 --> 00:05:28.039
- Who's that?

00:05:28.039 --> 00:05:29.027
- [Kelly] He was in choir with me.

00:05:29.027 --> 00:05:30.136
And I was like, if you sing...

00:05:30.136 --> 00:05:32.256
♪ Five hundred, 25,000 ♪

00:05:32.256 --> 00:05:34.387
I was like, "If I hear it one more time,

00:05:34.387 --> 00:05:35.564
I'm going to shoot myself".

00:05:35.564 --> 00:05:38.196
- I know, I know, it can
all get a bit overbearing.

00:05:38.196 --> 00:05:40.067
- No, it was, it's just,
if that was the musical,

00:05:40.067 --> 00:05:41.678
when I was in high school
that everyone's sang,

00:05:41.678 --> 00:05:43.096
at every audition that I was like,

00:05:43.096 --> 00:05:44.836
"I can't, I can't hear it again".

00:05:44.836 --> 00:05:46.176
(Kelly and Colin laugh)

00:05:46.176 --> 00:05:47.726
But then I ended up going
to see my friend on it,

00:05:47.726 --> 00:05:49.166
on Broadway, it was, it's amazing.

00:05:49.166 --> 00:05:50.398
- Yeah and I saw the original cast,

00:05:50.398 --> 00:05:51.906
in London with my brother.

00:05:51.906 --> 00:05:53.273
- [Kelly] Bragger.

00:05:53.273 --> 00:05:55.315
- And like we went and
had a bunch of margaritas

00:05:55.315 --> 00:05:57.275
and got well oiled and
then went and saw that.

00:05:57.275 --> 00:05:58.704
- Well oiled.
(Kelly laughs)

00:05:58.704 --> 00:06:00.195
(Colin mumbles)
- You know?

00:06:00.195 --> 00:06:01.382
- But this may sound weird,

00:06:01.382 --> 00:06:03.054
but I have to ask about your cat.

00:06:03.054 --> 00:06:06.046
Because you look like Dr.
Evil in an interview recently.

00:06:06.046 --> 00:06:06.879
(Kelly laughs)

00:06:06.879 --> 00:06:09.414
You did an interview and you
had your cat on your lap.

00:06:09.414 --> 00:06:10.544
I was like, and I,

00:06:10.544 --> 00:06:11.744
the internet wouldn't
stop talking about it,

00:06:11.744 --> 00:06:12.577
neither would I.

00:06:12.577 --> 00:06:13.714
Here's a look, if you missed it.

00:06:13.714 --> 00:06:14.674
- [Colin] Oh.
(audience and Colin laugh)

00:06:14.674 --> 00:06:16.515
I look like I'm panicking,
why am I so afraid?

00:06:16.515 --> 00:06:17.348
(Kelly and audience laugh)

00:06:17.348 --> 00:06:19.854
It looks like the cat might've
just... (beeping) On me.

00:06:19.854 --> 00:06:21.704
- Oh my God, I love cats by
the way, I grew up with them.

00:06:21.704 --> 00:06:22.537
- I love cats too.

00:06:22.537 --> 00:06:23.370
- Yeah, how many do you have?

00:06:23.370 --> 00:06:24.203
- [Colin] Someone, someone said to me,

00:06:24.203 --> 00:06:25.766
we saw a thing of a cat, not this,

00:06:25.766 --> 00:06:26.955
but something else with a cat.

00:06:26.955 --> 00:06:28.504
they heard I had a cat and they said,

00:06:28.504 --> 00:06:30.357
"We thought you were a dog
person". It's like... (beeping)

00:06:30.357 --> 00:06:31.190
Can we just human beings,

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:33.555
not actually put lines
in the sand for once?

00:06:33.555 --> 00:06:34.493
(Kelly and audience laugh)

00:06:34.493 --> 00:06:35.422
- Jesus...

00:06:35.422 --> 00:06:36.510
- I can like both.
(audience applauds)

00:06:36.510 --> 00:06:38.914
- Totally, I'm like, "No, I always thought

00:06:38.914 --> 00:06:40.343
I was a dog person as well".

00:06:40.343 --> 00:06:42.003
So, I was guilty of self-judgment.

00:06:42.003 --> 00:06:45.251
But apparently I can, as
you said, I can love both.

00:06:45.251 --> 00:06:46.084
Cats, of course.

00:06:46.084 --> 00:06:47.611
I have two cats now,
they're brother and sister,

00:06:47.611 --> 00:06:48.444
two rescues.

00:06:48.444 --> 00:06:49.277
- Aw.

00:06:49.277 --> 00:06:50.110
- [Colin] Murphy and Mia.

00:06:50.110 --> 00:06:50.943
And they're cool man.

00:06:50.943 --> 00:06:51.776
- [Kelly] Murphy and Mia.

00:06:51.776 --> 00:06:52.609
- Yeah, Murphy and Mia.

00:06:52.609 --> 00:06:54.110
Mia's is a bit, a bit...

00:06:54.110 --> 00:06:54.943
- [Kelly] Sassy?

00:06:54.943 --> 00:06:55.776
- She's neurotic.
(audience laughs)

00:06:55.776 --> 00:06:57.451
She just destroys everything.

00:06:57.451 --> 00:06:59.588
- Oh my God, my sister, I love her cat.

00:06:59.588 --> 00:07:01.731
Her cat is old and it's a shame,

00:07:01.731 --> 00:07:04.563
will literally, I guess
walk up and just poo,

00:07:04.563 --> 00:07:05.396
right on her nightstand

00:07:05.396 --> 00:07:07.770
and then look at her
and then just walk off.

00:07:07.770 --> 00:07:08.603
(Kelly laughs)

00:07:08.603 --> 00:07:09.662
And I'm like, that's the
difference between cats and dogs.

00:07:09.662 --> 00:07:12.483
- We do not, they're the gifts
we do not want to receive.

00:07:12.483 --> 00:07:13.316
- [Kelly] It's awesome.

00:07:13.316 --> 00:07:15.771
I just, she hates it and
I love this cat so much,

00:07:15.771 --> 00:07:17.451
because it brings me joy.

00:07:17.451 --> 00:07:19.542
But I'm very, very
excited and so is Rubin,

00:07:19.542 --> 00:07:21.763
who loves superhero stuff more
than me and all that stuff.

00:07:21.763 --> 00:07:24.003
So, we're excited about "The Batman", so.

00:07:24.003 --> 00:07:24.853
(audience applauds)

00:07:24.853 --> 00:07:26.712
They're excited.

00:07:26.712 --> 00:07:28.932
So, what can you tell us about it?

00:07:28.932 --> 00:07:30.363
You play The Penguin.

00:07:30.363 --> 00:07:32.530
- I play, yeah, I play Oz.

00:07:34.081 --> 00:07:36.831
Who's kind of, hasn't
embodied The Penguin yet,

00:07:36.831 --> 00:07:38.392
but is known as The Penguin basically,

00:07:38.392 --> 00:07:41.975
because he has a bit
of a, an awkward gate.

00:07:44.522 --> 00:07:45.988
And yeah, it was, it was, it was...

00:07:45.988 --> 00:07:48.079
Oh yeah, there he is.

00:07:48.079 --> 00:07:49.608
A really extraordinary makeup artist,

00:07:49.608 --> 00:07:51.099
called, Mike Marino.

00:07:51.099 --> 00:07:52.419
Kind of designed the character.

00:07:52.419 --> 00:07:53.870
I would say, I can...
- Wait, wait, what?

00:07:53.870 --> 00:07:55.699
Wait, that's not you though?

00:07:55.699 --> 00:07:56.532
- Yeah.

00:07:56.532 --> 00:07:57.499
- Wait, what?

00:07:57.499 --> 00:07:58.646
- Yeah.

00:07:58.646 --> 00:08:01.619
- Wait, what?
(audience laughs)

00:08:01.619 --> 00:08:03.240
I didn't see that picture, oh my God.

00:08:03.240 --> 00:08:04.073
- [Colin] You didn't, really?

00:08:04.073 --> 00:08:04.906
- [Kelly] I just heard
that you were Penguin.

00:08:04.906 --> 00:08:06.179
What the hell?
- You haven't seen that?

00:08:06.179 --> 00:08:07.728
- [Kelly] That person
deserves to win awards.

00:08:07.728 --> 00:08:08.938
- [Colin] Oh, no, no, no, he should, yeah.

00:08:08.938 --> 00:08:10.160
(audience applauds)
Yeah, yeah.

00:08:10.160 --> 00:08:11.148
- [Kelly] That's you?

00:08:11.148 --> 00:08:12.270
- [Colin] No, it's amazing.

00:08:12.270 --> 00:08:14.808
It's amazing what he
was... And he designed,

00:08:14.808 --> 00:08:15.678
he designed the whole thing.

00:08:15.678 --> 00:08:16.869
- I couldn't download
the photo, last night.

00:08:16.869 --> 00:08:17.702
And I kept telling her, I was like,

00:08:17.702 --> 00:08:19.372
"I never saw him as Penguin".
- It's amazing.

00:08:19.372 --> 00:08:20.205
- [Kelly] Oh, my gosh.

00:08:20.205 --> 00:08:22.227
- The first time I saw the makeup,

00:08:22.227 --> 00:08:26.477
was they had done a, he
had done a mold of my face.

00:08:28.448 --> 00:08:30.531
And I saw it on a screen.

00:08:31.528 --> 00:08:33.707
Matt Reeves' screen, the director,

00:08:33.707 --> 00:08:35.496
the writer, director of "The Batman".

00:08:35.496 --> 00:08:37.568
He said, "You want to see
what Mike Marino's done?

00:08:37.568 --> 00:08:38.939
What he thinks, what he thinks
Oz is going to look like?"

00:08:38.939 --> 00:08:40.605
And I said, "Yeah". And
he showed me the screen,

00:08:40.605 --> 00:08:42.267
I just, I didn't know it
was going in that direction.

00:08:42.267 --> 00:08:43.666
And I went, "Holy smoke".

00:08:43.666 --> 00:08:46.278
And I'd never done
anything like that before.

00:08:46.278 --> 00:08:47.638
And I can't claim...

00:08:47.638 --> 00:08:48.747
- What kind of time did
it take to look like that?

00:08:48.747 --> 00:08:50.785
- Four hours, four hours.
(Kelly gasps)

00:08:50.785 --> 00:08:53.505
At the start, four hours and
then they got it down to two.

00:08:53.505 --> 00:08:54.425
And it was fine,

00:08:54.425 --> 00:08:57.374
because I knew that the reward
was immense and it was...

00:08:57.374 --> 00:08:58.625
- You're a different human is the...

00:08:58.625 --> 00:09:00.633
- It was extraordinary,
Kelly, it was so liberating.

00:09:00.633 --> 00:09:02.294
- Did you ever go out in that?

00:09:02.294 --> 00:09:04.582
- No, we did...
- I would've gone out in that.

00:09:04.582 --> 00:09:05.555
- We did a test.

00:09:05.555 --> 00:09:06.585
- And then talked...
(beeping)

00:09:06.585 --> 00:09:07.418
About Colin Ferrell.

00:09:07.418 --> 00:09:08.475
(Kelly and Colin laugh)

00:09:08.475 --> 00:09:11.202
- See what people really feel.

00:09:11.202 --> 00:09:12.035
Until you find out, they're like,

00:09:12.035 --> 00:09:12.944
"Sorry, never heard of him".

00:09:12.944 --> 00:09:14.131
Ooh, checked ego.

00:09:14.131 --> 00:09:15.973
(audience applauds)

00:09:15.973 --> 00:09:17.475
- That would've been what I would've done.

00:09:17.475 --> 00:09:18.308
- Yeah, that experiment backfired.

00:09:18.308 --> 00:09:20.795
(Kelly laughs)

00:09:20.795 --> 00:09:22.452
It was amazing, yeah.
- That's crazy.

00:09:22.452 --> 00:09:24.113
- So, I can,

00:09:24.113 --> 00:09:26.946
I've never been able to take less,

00:09:28.763 --> 00:09:32.411
ownership over a performance in my life.

00:09:32.411 --> 00:09:33.244
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:09:33.244 --> 00:09:34.461
It's like so physically different, yeah.

00:09:34.461 --> 00:09:35.891
- It's, it's like,

00:09:35.891 --> 00:09:38.968
I don't know if it's 50/50, 49/51,

00:09:38.968 --> 00:09:40.371
60/40, I'm not sure.

00:09:40.371 --> 00:09:41.204
- [Kelly] Oh, my gosh.

00:09:41.204 --> 00:09:43.171
- But Mike Marino and myself

00:09:43.171 --> 00:09:44.610
and then Matt of course wrote it.

00:09:44.610 --> 00:09:46.651
You know, it's, it's a,

00:09:46.651 --> 00:09:48.180
you didn't have to do much.

00:09:48.180 --> 00:09:49.013
- So intense.

00:09:49.013 --> 00:09:49.883
- [Colin] It was like an alchemy.

00:09:49.883 --> 00:09:51.173
Yeah, when it went on the first time

00:09:51.173 --> 00:09:54.421
and just, you're hidden and
you just have absolute freedom.

00:09:54.421 --> 00:09:57.053
- Oh my God, I will never
complain about spanks again.

00:09:57.053 --> 00:09:57.886
(audience and Colin laugh)

00:09:57.886 --> 00:10:01.081
When you have them on for
four hours, that is a lot.

00:10:01.081 --> 00:10:02.721
Okay so, I want to talk
about your other film.

00:10:02.721 --> 00:10:03.682
Because one wasn't enough for you to do.

00:10:03.682 --> 00:10:04.515
- Yeah, "After Yang".

00:10:04.515 --> 00:10:05.348
- [Kelly] "After Yang".

00:10:05.348 --> 00:10:06.181
So, what's it about?

00:10:06.181 --> 00:10:08.952
- Greedy, "After Yang" is about a family,

00:10:08.952 --> 00:10:12.282
going through, that family there,

00:10:12.282 --> 00:10:13.283
going through...
- Beautiful family.

00:10:13.283 --> 00:10:17.293
A version of a, of a kind
of, a crisis in a way.

00:10:17.293 --> 00:10:20.901
It is an undescribed time in the future.

00:10:20.901 --> 00:10:23.661
And it is a time on our planet,

00:10:23.661 --> 00:10:26.889
where technology has
reached the stage where

00:10:26.889 --> 00:10:29.222
you can have a living robot.

00:10:30.471 --> 00:10:33.281
What we call it in the
film is "technosapiens".

00:10:33.281 --> 00:10:35.831
And myself and my wife,

00:10:35.831 --> 00:10:37.281
played by Jodie Turner Smith,

00:10:37.281 --> 00:10:42.031
have an adopted daughter who
comes from Chinese heritage.

00:10:43.776 --> 00:10:48.380
And we have this technosapien
to be a sibling to her.

00:10:48.380 --> 00:10:52.191
And to also be a reference point for her.

00:10:52.191 --> 00:10:53.024
- Like culturally?

00:10:53.024 --> 00:10:54.460
- Yeah, her cultural information,

00:10:54.460 --> 00:10:56.100
that she wouldn't get otherwise.

00:10:56.100 --> 00:10:56.951
And the film opens up,

00:10:56.951 --> 00:10:58.351
basically you see the family together

00:10:58.351 --> 00:11:01.281
and then very quickly the
technosapien breaks down.

00:11:01.281 --> 00:11:03.071
And it's about, the film is about grief

00:11:03.071 --> 00:11:05.601
and about loss and about
family and about memory.

00:11:05.601 --> 00:11:07.220
And I suppose to me, I don't know,

00:11:07.220 --> 00:11:09.612
it's about the important moments in life.

00:11:09.612 --> 00:11:11.972
The simple moments that
we can so easily overlook,

00:11:11.972 --> 00:11:15.100
in striving for something that
we think will hold meaning,

00:11:15.100 --> 00:11:16.340
that's outside of our experience.

00:11:16.340 --> 00:11:17.972
Something that we think
will make us happy,

00:11:17.972 --> 00:11:19.391
something that we think we can achieve

00:11:19.391 --> 00:11:20.481
and will answer all our problems.

00:11:20.481 --> 00:11:21.314
When in fact...
- Oh, Lord.

00:11:21.314 --> 00:11:22.161
- We have so much...

00:11:22.161 --> 00:11:23.481
- Have you snuck into my therapy sessions?

00:11:23.481 --> 00:11:24.500
(Colin and Kelly laugh)

00:11:24.500 --> 00:11:25.380
I'm like, "Wait, what?"

00:11:25.380 --> 00:11:27.660
- [Colin] Yeah, yeah, so you
and me, both. I read it and it,

00:11:27.660 --> 00:11:30.748
it hit me, reading the script fairly hard.

00:11:30.748 --> 00:11:32.081
Because it was just so
beautifully written,

00:11:32.081 --> 00:11:34.481
by the director as well, Kogonada,

00:11:34.481 --> 00:11:36.460
he wrote the script
based on a short story.

00:11:36.460 --> 00:11:37.780
- I love that you're doing two films.

00:11:37.780 --> 00:11:40.617
You're promoting two films
and they're so different.

00:11:40.617 --> 00:11:41.450
- Yeah and to be honest with you,

00:11:41.450 --> 00:11:42.283
like "The Batman", you know,

00:11:42.283 --> 00:11:43.281
it's great to do press for it and all,

00:11:43.281 --> 00:11:44.862
but look, there's trailers everywhere

00:11:44.862 --> 00:11:46.244
and there'll be posters everywhere.

00:11:46.244 --> 00:11:48.462
And "After Yang" hasn't
really got much of a nickel

00:11:48.462 --> 00:11:49.462
to put into stuff.

00:11:49.462 --> 00:11:51.574
And it's a small film and it, you know,

00:11:51.574 --> 00:11:53.364
it's not, it's not a summer blockbuster.

00:11:53.364 --> 00:11:55.006
- [Kelly] But it seems poignant
and the message is on point.

00:11:55.006 --> 00:11:56.974
- I think so, you know,
and people seem to,

00:11:56.974 --> 00:11:58.153
it premiered in Sundance

00:11:58.153 --> 00:12:00.524
and people had some very
emotional responses too,

00:12:00.524 --> 00:12:02.524
which is unusual for me,
or anything I'm part of.

00:12:02.524 --> 00:12:03.357
- What?

00:12:03.357 --> 00:12:04.942
- It's nice, yeah, you know, I don't do,

00:12:04.942 --> 00:12:07.740
well, a lot of stuff I've done
has kind of been violent or.

00:12:07.740 --> 00:12:08.573
- [Kelly] I love that about you.

00:12:08.573 --> 00:12:09.406
I love, that's what I
was just about to say.

00:12:09.406 --> 00:12:10.418
- You love my violence?

00:12:10.418 --> 00:12:12.026
- No, I love that like, you'll
be in those films though,

00:12:12.026 --> 00:12:14.167
but you'll also do, I like
the fact that you just,

00:12:14.167 --> 00:12:15.775
even these two films that
you, the juxtaposition...

00:12:15.775 --> 00:12:16.608
- [Colin] And it's fun.

00:12:16.608 --> 00:12:17.441
- It's cool.

00:12:17.441 --> 00:12:18.274
- It's fun, honest to God, it's fun.

00:12:18.274 --> 00:12:20.026
It is fun, it's just us,

00:12:20.026 --> 00:12:20.859
It's just really fun.

00:12:20.859 --> 00:12:22.676
I'm just spoiled, just get
to do different things...

00:12:22.676 --> 00:12:24.364
- You're a completely different
human in "The Batman".

00:12:24.364 --> 00:12:25.197
(Kelly laughs)

00:12:25.197 --> 00:12:26.863
- Yeah, yeah, yeah. No,
it's fun, love, for me.

00:12:26.863 --> 00:12:28.564
- Remember that time I thought
they put someone else up?

00:12:28.564 --> 00:12:29.546
(Kelly laughs)
- Yeah.

00:12:29.546 --> 00:12:30.852
- [Kelly] I was like, "This is rude".

